Subject: [PATCH] dns: close completed TCP streams after draining replies

A clean EOF from DNS hijacking is reported as success, so the caller's
handshake-error cleanup leaves the connection open. Native TUN retains
these flows in CLOSE_WAIT while peer probes keep refreshing conntrack.

Share the DNS stream loop between its existing callers. Drain accepted
asynchronous replies on a clean EOF before closing the stream, with the
existing DNS timeout bounding response writes. Keep error cleanup and
close callbacks in the existing callers.

